    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the manual says e15 means there's a leak in the base tray. i dont see any water on the kitchen floor though. how do i check the sensor at the bottom and how do i dry it out?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If the manual points to a leak in the base tray, even if the floor is dry, the leak might be internal, perhaps near the pump area, which is a tricky spot to check without disassembly. You'll need to locate the water level sensor or float switch, which is usually near the bottom of the tub. To check it, you might need to carefully pull out the lower rack and look underneath for the sensor assembly. Gently wipe the sensor clean with a dry cloth, ensuring no residual water or soap scum is interfering with its function, as a damp sensor can trigger a leak code even if there's no active drip.",
